\newlabel{tab:t3metrics}{{4}{12}{Track~3 trajectory metrics, descriptive, not registered (\texttt {scripts/t3\_metrics.py}, from stored evaluation episodes only; no new runs). Rows pool the arm's seeds (models column). Arms: Dw, the recovery-SFT warm start; A, the RSC GRPO agent; D, Dw then GRPO; Dw\_aug, the augmented warm start; B0 and B4, scripts. \emph {Success}: verified success VSC (P1, P4, AD-C1) or verified transaction completion VTC (TXN), greedy and sampled ($T=1$) episodes separately. \emph {Tool acc.}: $1-$invalid$/$policy calls, pooled over all episodes; invalid = unknown tool, arguments that do not bind to the tool signature, or arguments that are not valid JSON; policy calls exclude the scripted start prefix. A turn without a parseable call ends the episode and is not a call. \emph {Calls}, \emph {turns}: per episode, all episodes. \emph {Wall s/ep}: the run's evaluation wall time divided by its episodes (range over runs); each run is one batched vLLM job, so this is throughput time per episode on the named GPU, not per-request latency, and it depends on the GPU, batch size and output length. Scripted policies (B0, B4) have no model turns or timed runs. \emph {Lower block}: the only measured per-episode latency (batch 1, one task at a time, greedy, 40 \texttt {proc\_dev} episodes, \texttt {scripts/latency\_proc.py}); of the models above, only the warm start's weights were timed this way (they are the AD-C1 warm start and arm A's base). D, Dw and Dw\_aug have no batch-1 measurement}{table.caption.30}{}}
